<title>VENEZUELA: Vencemos affiliate to issue $20 mln 5 yr euro.</title>
<headline>Vencemos affiliate to issue $20 mln 5 yr euro.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vencemos Financial Corporation, an affiliate of Venezuelan cement company Vencemos, will go to market July 1 with a five year $20 million euro bond, lead agent Merinvest told Reuters.</p>
<p>The bond, to be used to restructure short term debt,  will carry an 8.5 percent coupon, with payments guaranteed by Venecemos, senior Merinvest advisor Alfonso Ortega said.</p>
<p>Venecomos is a subsidiary of Mexican cement giant Cemex .</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
